WEBVTT

00:15.670 --> 00:18.500
I never dreamed before

00:18.500 --> 00:21.340
I'm gonna knock the door

00:21.340 --> 00:24.910
into the world of perfect free

00:24.910 --> 00:27.010
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:27.010 --> 00:29.850
You're gonna say I'm lying

00:29.850 --> 00:32.580
I'm gonna get the chance

00:32.580 --> 00:36.150
I thought a chance is far from me

00:36.150 --> 00:37.320
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:37.320 --> 00:40.230
I was made to hit in America

00:40.230 --> 00:43.090
(I was made to hit in America)

00:43.090 --> 00:49.000
I was made to hit in America

00:49.000 --> 00:52.670
You are the sun, you are the star

00:52.670 --> 00:54.670
(To me, forever)

00:54.670 --> 00:58.380
You are the sun, you are the star

00:58.380 --> 01:01.370
(To me, forever)

01:08.450 --> 01:14.060
I was made to hit in America

01:14.060 --> 01:16.900
I was made to hit in America

01:16.900 --> 01:19.760
(I was made to hit in America)

01:19.760 --> 01:22.570
I was made to hit in America

01:22.570 --> 01:25.340
(I was made to hit in America)

01:25.340 --> 01:33.010
I was made to hit in America

01:46.060 --> 01:51.720
Ryusuke. I'm going to form
the ultimate band.

01:57.640 --> 01:59.400
So will I.

02:16.960 --> 02:18.360
Umm...

02:18.360 --> 02:22.090
I was hoping to borrow that
Dying Breed CD from their indie days.

02:23.400 --> 02:26.730
Koyuki. If you have time, follow me.

02:52.490 --> 02:56.090
Ryusuke-kun, how's the guitar?

02:56.090 --> 02:59.630
-Concentrate on the sound.
-Sound?

02:59.630 --> 03:02.790
Close your eyes and focus on the sound.

03:09.540 --> 03:13.910
Can you hear the bass?
The level is different.

03:35.070 --> 03:38.940
Yeah, yeah. Yeah, I'm about to go there.

03:38.940 --> 03:42.410
Well, don't get pissed.
Okay, I'll be there.

03:42.410 --> 03:44.240
Ryusuke-kun, is something wrong?

03:44.240 --> 03:47.150
Yeah, something came up.

03:47.150 --> 03:51.050
He was awfully mad.

03:51.050 --> 03:54.090
Didn't you hear me? I said no thanks.

03:54.090 --> 03:56.850
I told you I'm just waiting for my brother,

03:56.850 --> 03:58.790
not for fuckin' guys like you.

03:58.790 --> 04:01.430
I'm not a whore like you think!

04:01.430 --> 04:03.860
No, I didn't mean it! Sorry.

04:03.860 --> 04:07.000
Bullshit, you fuckin' bastard! Go away!

04:07.000 --> 04:10.600
Wow...You're too scary.

04:10.600 --> 04:14.440
Scary?! Who do you think makes me scary?

04:19.110 --> 04:21.180
Hey, what's going on? Who are they?

04:21.180 --> 04:25.480
Well, they were hitting on me.
They should go to hell.

04:25.480 --> 04:27.550
They're both freaked out like shit.

04:27.550 --> 04:28.850
'Cuz you're late!

04:28.850 --> 04:31.010
Well, sorry about that.

04:38.200 --> 04:40.300
Oh, yeah. Let me introduce you.

04:40.300 --> 04:43.270
Koyuki is 14, same as you, Maho.

04:43.270 --> 04:44.400
I know!

04:44.400 --> 04:47.770
-And what'll you have?
-Whatever.

04:47.770 --> 04:51.380
Okay, then. Koyuki, take care of it.

04:51.380 --> 04:53.610
I'm going to talk to Taira, the bassist.

04:53.610 --> 04:57.980
I've gotta catch him early,
or he'll be taken.

04:57.980 --> 05:02.890
The main thing in a band is...
a bassist and drummer.

05:02.890 --> 05:04.720
Is a beef bowl okay?

05:12.960 --> 05:15.830
Okay, see you later.

05:15.830 --> 05:18.670
I called some friends from school.
You don't mind, do you?

05:18.670 --> 05:20.330
Sure.

05:23.140 --> 05:27.780
Say, the other day, I met this guy,
and he tried to pick me up!

05:27.780 --> 05:30.050
But he was such an asshole!

05:30.050 --> 05:32.380
But he had a BMW convertible!

05:32.380 --> 05:35.890
Really? That's cool! I love that car!

05:35.890 --> 05:38.690
I know...But he was awfully creepy!

05:38.690 --> 05:42.150
His eyes twitched in this weird way
and it made me sick!

05:44.630 --> 05:47.060
But Risa, you always
get stuck with weirdos.

05:47.060 --> 05:48.070
I know...

05:48.070 --> 05:51.140
Why don't you wait for Maho's rejects?

05:51.140 --> 05:53.170
Oh no. Some poor-looking foreigners
hit on me earlier.

05:53.170 --> 05:56.640
-Poor foreigners? That sucks!
-Yeah...

05:56.640 --> 06:00.270
There's never cool guys.
I like guys riding Porsches.

06:01.710 --> 06:04.150
-Then I want a Ferrari.
-Me too!

06:05.350 --> 06:08.250
Hey, let's go clubbing now.
We might find our dream guy.

06:08.250 --> 06:10.290
Yay, let's go!

06:10.290 --> 06:12.990
Yeah, I wanna go, but I'm broke.

06:12.990 --> 06:14.530
-Umm...I...
-Come on!

06:14.530 --> 06:16.530
Fine, the dream guy will pay for you.

06:16.530 --> 06:19.300
Yeah, free buy!

06:19.300 --> 06:22.960
I have something to
take care of, so I'll be going.

06:28.670 --> 06:32.630
They don't teach English properly
in Japan, is what I feel.

06:33.880 --> 06:35.750
Dutch, huh?

06:35.750 --> 06:38.320
Your Japanese has improved.

06:38.320 --> 06:40.380
Is that meant to be a compliment?

06:42.050 --> 06:45.020
Eiji and I jammed the other day.

06:46.760 --> 06:49.620
He's getting better, amazingly fast.

06:52.030 --> 06:57.130
I finish school this year,
and I'm thinking seriously about my future.

06:57.130 --> 07:00.230
If you want to make music with me,
bring me a really great vocalist.

07:15.420 --> 07:17.220
A vocalist, huh?

07:33.100 --> 07:34.440
Yo!

07:37.240 --> 07:38.880
W-what happened?

07:38.880 --> 07:42.870
I have no place to crash tonight.
So I'm going to Ryusuke's place.

07:44.980 --> 07:46.810
Umm, the other day...

07:48.650 --> 07:52.060
I'm sorry I laughed at you
about not knowing kanji.

07:52.060 --> 07:56.530
Don't worry about it.
Besides, I am bad at kanji.

07:56.530 --> 07:59.930
I got fired from a diner yesterday
because I didn't know the language.

07:59.930 --> 08:00.700
Are you serious?

08:00.700 --> 08:05.360
I was so mad, I yelled and cried
that I was going back to America.

08:09.140 --> 08:11.040
Then my dad slapped me.

08:12.310 --> 08:13.870
Are you all right?

08:18.080 --> 08:20.180
You're very kind, Koyuki.

08:22.090 --> 08:25.360
But you don't seem to like my friends.

08:25.360 --> 08:28.460
B-because I left early?

08:28.460 --> 08:31.460
You didn't try to talk to them.

08:31.460 --> 08:35.830
-But the language...
-ls that it? The language?

08:35.830 --> 08:38.200
Everyone says the same thing.

08:38.200 --> 08:39.970
Well, let's go see Beck!

08:39.970 --> 08:42.440
Huh? Beck?!

08:44.840 --> 08:46.240
Beck!

08:58.660 --> 09:02.330
Hey, Beck! I haven't seen you
in a while, yet you ignore me!

09:02.330 --> 09:04.630
Please help me, Maho-chan!

09:04.630 --> 09:06.720
Stop adding "-chan" to my name.

09:10.130 --> 09:12.170
Hi, Beck...

09:12.170 --> 09:13.800
How's it going?

09:15.510 --> 09:18.000
Brother taking care of you?

09:20.310 --> 09:22.540
Such a pretty full moon.

09:25.920 --> 09:28.090
It's a full moon tonight.

09:28.090 --> 09:33.680
Full moon sways...

09:35.190 --> 09:40.650
Gently in the night of one fine day...

09:43.030 --> 09:47.770
Maho, you're amazing. You can
speak English and you sing great.

09:47.770 --> 09:49.240
And you're cute...

09:49.240 --> 09:51.140
I know you'll make it as a singer!

09:51.140 --> 09:52.380
As if!

09:52.380 --> 09:56.050
I have no talent as a singer.

09:56.050 --> 09:59.950
My dream is to study movies in New York.

10:11.130 --> 10:18.800
Full moon sways...

10:18.800 --> 10:25.470
Gently in the night of one fine day.

10:26.980 --> 10:33.440
On my way...

10:34.790 --> 10:41.710
Looking for a moment with my dear...

10:49.470 --> 10:52.660
It's my favorite song by Dying Breed.

11:11.920 --> 11:13.720
Hey, Tanaka!

11:19.030 --> 11:20.630
Find something?

11:20.630 --> 11:24.860
Oh, it's you, Izumi-chan!
Don't scare me like that!

11:26.200 --> 11:29.270
-So, are you willing?
-Huh?

11:29.270 --> 11:33.180
Stop by the municipal pool at 6 pm.

11:33.180 --> 11:35.180
Pool?

11:35.180 --> 11:38.910
Don't be late, now.
You'll find out when you get there.

11:40.420 --> 11:42.180
The municipal pool?

11:46.490 --> 11:48.290
Well then, I'll see you later.

11:48.290 --> 11:49.090
"Business envelopes, fabric tape,
aluminum foil, polyester bags"

11:49.090 --> 11:50.260
"Business envelopes, fabric tape,
aluminum foil, polyester bags"

11:49.090 --> 11:50.260
Please consider the financing!

11:50.260 --> 11:52.750
Please consider the financing!

11:53.630 --> 11:56.430
Please! Thank you!

11:56.430 --> 11:57.500
"Saito Paper Company"

11:56.430 --> 11:57.500
Please! Thank you!

11:57.500 --> 11:59.260
"Saito Paper Company"

12:03.440 --> 12:05.940
5:30 huh?

12:05.940 --> 12:07.670
There!

12:09.410 --> 12:11.380
And now...

12:20.060 --> 12:22.830
Hey, kid...

12:22.830 --> 12:26.130
Please don't grab onto the lane ropes.

12:26.130 --> 12:29.170
I know, but...

12:29.170 --> 12:35.470
Hey, kid! If you're in the
50 meter pool, don't stop!

12:49.020 --> 12:53.160
-There he is.
-Let's go home.

12:53.160 --> 12:55.790
Hey, your kick is okay,

12:55.790 --> 13:00.130
but you pull with your elbow,
so you're not cutting into the water.

13:00.130 --> 13:02.170
Huh? Oh...

13:02.170 --> 13:05.620
Okay! Hook your feet
against the pool and practice!

13:07.240 --> 13:10.870
-Let's give it a try!
-W-who is he?

13:10.870 --> 13:13.810
He's the famous man of this pool.

13:13.810 --> 13:15.180
Famous?

13:15.180 --> 13:19.380
His name's Saito-san, and he
was once an Olympic swimmer.

13:19.380 --> 13:23.690
So whenever he sees a poor swimmer,
he can't help but teach.

13:23.690 --> 13:25.290
An Olympic swimmer?

13:25.290 --> 13:28.220
Well, he's not a bad guy.

13:31.100 --> 13:34.500
Huh? That's strange...

13:34.500 --> 13:36.470
Izumi!

13:36.470 --> 13:39.400
He's in the 25-meter pool.

13:39.400 --> 13:44.510
One, two, three, four...

13:44.510 --> 13:47.080
Just as I figured!

13:47.080 --> 13:50.150
Koyuki got caught!

13:50.150 --> 13:53.580
Kid, are you ready?

13:53.580 --> 13:55.690
You're giving me a
15-meter handicap, right?

13:55.690 --> 14:00.290
Yeah...This is serious, a real contest.

14:00.290 --> 14:02.930
Yes. And if I win?

14:02.930 --> 14:07.000
As promised, I'll train you man to man.

14:07.000 --> 14:07.700
All right.

14:07.700 --> 14:10.700
-And if you lose...
-lf I lose?

14:10.700 --> 14:12.170
I'll hit you!

14:13.600 --> 14:17.840
Huh?!

14:17.840 --> 14:20.610
And I won't hold back!

14:20.610 --> 14:21.880
Why would you do that?!

14:21.880 --> 14:27.050
Kid...In the grown-up world,
there are many painful things!

14:27.050 --> 14:29.550
Now get set!

14:29.550 --> 14:31.280
Ready!

14:32.520 --> 14:33.960
Go!

14:38.330 --> 14:39.920
Five meters.

14:41.630 --> 14:43.220
Ten meters.

14:44.900 --> 14:48.770
Fifteen meters!

14:58.750 --> 15:01.310
Victory is mine!

15:13.400 --> 15:15.630
I...did it!

15:17.470 --> 15:18.870
Saito-san...

15:20.540 --> 15:22.070
It's been a long time.

15:22.070 --> 15:23.600
Izumi-chan!

15:27.010 --> 15:27.780
Oh!

15:27.780 --> 15:32.220
You're in the swim club at my alma mater,
Ihara East Middle School!

15:32.220 --> 15:34.820
How is Suzuki-sensei's lumbago?

15:34.820 --> 15:37.290
I think it's much better.

15:37.290 --> 15:39.790
Saito-san, please come
and coach us again!

15:39.790 --> 15:43.590
Oh, really? I'm glad that
someone like you appreciates me!

15:46.760 --> 15:49.970
-Then you talked to him?
-Yeah.

15:49.970 --> 15:51.460
You're really...

15:52.600 --> 15:56.740
I asked him for some advice. And then...

15:56.740 --> 15:58.840
And then?

15:58.840 --> 16:03.180
We somehow wound up in a race.

16:03.180 --> 16:04.410
Koyuki-kun!

16:06.420 --> 16:07.850
Want some?

16:07.850 --> 16:10.420
-N-no, thank you.
-No?

16:10.420 --> 16:14.690
Well, let's practice again tomorrow!
Good night!

16:18.430 --> 16:20.360
He's like a different person.

16:22.000 --> 16:25.330
Saito-san is a really warm-hearted
gentleman outside the pool.

16:27.540 --> 16:31.810
He listens to U.K. Rock bands, I think.

16:31.810 --> 16:33.180
U.K.?

16:33.180 --> 16:37.850
English rock bands.
Like the Beatles and stuff.

16:37.850 --> 16:40.050
The Stones are British, too, right?

16:40.050 --> 16:43.450
Yes, the Zeppelin too.

16:43.450 --> 16:45.390
I feel like I'm in the way.

16:45.390 --> 16:47.020
Huh?

16:47.020 --> 16:50.460
I have an early curfew. Good night!

16:53.460 --> 16:57.400
-Is swimming fun?
-Yeah.

16:57.400 --> 17:00.500
-Think you'll continue?
-Yeah.

17:00.500 --> 17:02.560
Really? I'm glad.

17:04.510 --> 17:08.650
I was going to stop by
Ryusuke-kun's place.

17:08.650 --> 17:10.770
Maybe I'll join you.

17:17.690 --> 17:19.660
You have a game on Sunday?

17:19.660 --> 17:21.730
Yeah, Mit-chan asked me.

17:21.730 --> 17:23.630
Umm...your grip...

17:25.230 --> 17:29.600
-He just needed a player...
-Ryusuke-kun, your grip...

17:29.600 --> 17:31.970
Huh? You say something, Koyuki?

17:31.970 --> 17:36.070
Koyuki has a present for you, Ryusuke-kun.

17:36.070 --> 17:37.540
A present?

17:39.510 --> 17:42.480
An unleashed dog may be taken away.

17:42.480 --> 17:47.250
I have been worried
how he doesn't come home lately...

17:50.150 --> 17:51.480
Wait a minute.

17:55.490 --> 17:57.320
Damn, it's dusty.

17:59.760 --> 18:02.730
You can have this.

18:02.730 --> 18:03.530
No way!

18:03.530 --> 18:06.600
You've been listening
to a lot of music lately.

18:06.600 --> 18:09.660
I figured you might want to play, too.

18:10.770 --> 18:13.140
It looks quite old.

18:17.410 --> 18:20.650
It's not much, but the sound is good.

18:20.650 --> 18:22.520
Wow!

18:22.520 --> 18:24.210
There we go.

18:57.620 --> 19:01.160
-A string broke.
-What song was that?

19:01.160 --> 19:03.930
-I just played whatever.
-It's the blues, right?

19:03.930 --> 19:05.200
Yeah.

19:05.200 --> 19:08.100
I love the way you play, Ryusuke-kun.

19:11.640 --> 19:17.070
I'm gonna play every waking moment
and get better and better!

19:17.070 --> 19:19.170
Huh? Yeah.

19:23.080 --> 19:27.450
Oh, Ryusuke-kun!
Mit-chan is steaming mad!

19:27.450 --> 19:30.950
-Wasn't it at 4:30?
-No, 3:00!

19:30.950 --> 19:32.620
It's already the last inning!

19:32.620 --> 19:34.020
I heard 4:30.

19:37.990 --> 19:39.900
Who's that pitcher?

19:39.900 --> 19:43.270
The vocalist for The Crowd,
Manabu Miyazawa.

19:43.270 --> 19:44.700
Is he famous?

19:44.700 --> 19:46.600
The Crowd had a huge following

19:46.600 --> 19:49.810
and people thought it was
a matter of time before they debuted.

19:49.810 --> 19:53.280
But the drummer suddenly quit
and the band broke up.

19:53.280 --> 19:56.010
The end was really pitiful.

20:00.880 --> 20:03.390
-Hey! Where're you throwing?!
-Oops! That's weird!

20:03.390 --> 20:05.350
I can't hit the bat!

20:06.360 --> 20:09.120
Batter! Don't move too much!

20:14.830 --> 20:17.630
-Strike!
-He doesn't seem so great...

20:17.630 --> 20:22.610
If he joins my band,
Taira-kun will join, too.

20:22.610 --> 20:26.810
Ryusuke-kun...Look at the other bench.

20:26.810 --> 20:28.750
Eiji...

20:28.750 --> 20:33.750
He's been asking Manabu-kun
to join since the Serial Mama stuff.

20:33.750 --> 20:35.290
Hey, Ryusuke!

20:35.290 --> 20:39.020
-Do you know what time it is?!
-Sorry, I had the wrong time.

20:39.020 --> 20:41.730
I told you we had just enough players.

20:41.730 --> 20:42.530
Sorry.

20:42.530 --> 20:47.830
'Cuz of you, I had to call the
one person in the world I didn't wanna.

20:47.830 --> 20:50.960
Not...Chiba?

20:53.900 --> 20:55.740
Ryusuke-kun?

20:55.740 --> 21:01.280
-I owe him 30,000 yen.
-Hey! Where's my money?!

21:01.280 --> 21:04.110
"Pay when you can."
Don't they have that in Japan?

21:04.110 --> 21:06.950
Shut up! You ingrate!

21:06.950 --> 21:12.460
Chiba! We only have the field
'til 5:00! Hurry it up!

21:12.460 --> 21:15.260
Just you wait, Ryusuke.

21:15.260 --> 21:16.380
Awright!

21:18.660 --> 21:19.820
Ball!

21:21.400 --> 21:24.730
Frankly, I don't care for Manabu's vocals.

21:24.730 --> 21:28.070
But in order to get Taira-kun,
I have no choice.

21:28.070 --> 21:32.980
-Then what about Chiba?
-Huh? I've never heard him sing.

21:32.980 --> 21:37.080
Chiba has charisma. He has
more aura than Manabu-kun.

21:37.080 --> 21:38.880
Oww!

21:39.820 --> 21:42.550
You should've moved!

21:44.020 --> 21:46.520
Dammit! I'll kill you!

21:46.520 --> 21:49.590
Oh, c'mon, don't get so uptight.

21:49.590 --> 21:52.100
You're the losers anyway.

21:52.100 --> 21:53.430
Calm down.

21:55.670 --> 21:58.430
Don't touch me!

22:00.100 --> 22:02.400
Oh well...

22:11.780 --> 22:13.310
Stop...

22:20.820 --> 22:28.320
Stop!

22:35.210 --> 22:37.070
Koyuki...

22:50.380 --> 22:52.480
Another minute

22:52.480 --> 22:55.350
Feelin' so fine

22:57.480 --> 22:59.720
You turn the freeze

22:59.720 --> 23:02.450
into warm light

23:04.560 --> 23:08.130
Had a premonition

23:08.130 --> 23:10.830
I've been waitin' ever since

23:10.830 --> 23:14.330
My world comin' down

23:14.330 --> 23:16.930
It's got me spinnin' 'round

23:18.910 --> 23:25.250
If you really wanna fly

23:25.250 --> 23:27.980
you gotta let go

23:40.090 --> 23:42.430
Simply the most

23:42.430 --> 23:44.460
big sensation

23:44.460 --> 23:47.270
(once you're here you won't go back)

23:47.270 --> 23:49.540
She's really pretty

23:49.540 --> 23:51.870
One-eyed vision

23:51.870 --> 23:54.370
(lose the fear it don't come back)

23:54.370 --> 23:58.040
Little sister showed me

23:58.040 --> 24:00.680
Really took me for a ride

24:00.680 --> 24:02.280
My world comin' down

24:02.280 --> 24:05.750
(once you're here you won't go back)

24:05.750 --> 24:09.710
(lose the fear it don't come back)

24:13.990 --> 24:16.300
I like Kasumi-chan of the tobacco shop.

24:16.300 --> 24:16.830
"Next Episode"

24:16.300 --> 24:16.830
I like Kasumi-chan of the tobacco shop.

24:16.830 --> 24:19.930
"Next Episode"

24:16.830 --> 24:19.930
But I also like Ranko-chan
of the family restaurant.

24:19.930 --> 24:20.230
"Next Episode"
